We've provided two storage devices that can be accessed at /dev/vdd and /dev/vde. Add these as physical volumes to LVM, then set up a volume group that includes both devices. Call this volume group VG1 (uppercase letters). On this volume group, add a logical volume of exactly 4.50 GB. Call this logical volume LV1 (uppercase letters).


Is /dev/vdd, /dev/vde added as physical volumes to the VG1 volume group ?

VG1 should be exactly this name (uppercase letters), and it shouldn't use <4.9 GB ?

Is logical volume should be called exactly LV1, created on VG1 with a size of 4.5 GB?


Solution
Create physical volumes on /dev/vdd and /dev/vde:

sudo pvcreate /dev/vdd /dev/vde

Create a volume group named VG1 that includes both /dev/vdb and /dev/vdc:

sudo vgcreate VG1 /dev/vdd /dev/vde

Create a logical volume named LV1 of exactly 4.50 GB within the VG1 volume group:

sudo lvcreate -L 4.50G -n LV1 VG1



